course: dictionary
lesson: 734
title: Basin: a bowl, a sink, or a river's land
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and basin is a good example. You work out which meaning is meant by reading the words around it, which are its context. «Wash your hands in the basin» is about a sink, but in a geography book a basin is a large area of land.
explain: The clue words tell you which meaning fits. «A pudding basin» is a deep bowl you use in the kitchen. «The Amazon basin» is an area of land. Ask yourself what would fit in the sentence, then put your meaning in place of the word and check that it still makes sense.
explain: A river basin is all the land where rain flows into one river. «A great river collects rain from a huge area, called its basin» tells you this. The land around the river slopes down towards it, so the basin is like a giant bowl that the river collects water from.
explain: Sometimes a sentence uses a picture to explain. «All the Sea rose up as water rises in a basin when you put your hand into it» compares the sea to water in a bowl. You do not need the sea to be a bowl; the comparison helps you picture how the water moves.
fact: Basin has several meanings, so check the sentence to find the right one.
fact: A basin can be a round bowl for mixing or washing food.
fact: A washbasin is a sink in a bathroom, where you wash your hands.
fact: In geography, a river basin is the land drained by a river and its streams, like «the Amazon basin».
fact: A «watershed» is the high land between two basins.
exercise: «Wash your hands in the basin.» In this sentence, what is a basin? | *A sink in a bathroom | A kind of river fish | A mountain peak | A large cake
exercise: «The Amazon basin has well over two thousand known kinds of fish.» What is the Amazon basin? | *The land drained by the Amazon river and its streams | A type of fish | A bowl for cooking | A tiny pond in a garden
exercise: «The line of high land between two basins is a watershed.» What is a watershed? | A waterfall that falls into the sea | A type of rainforest | A pudding bowl | *The high land between two basins
test: «She mixed the cake in a large pudding basin.» What does basin mean here? | *A deep bowl for mixing | A river with fish in it | A shower for washing | A large lake
test: «Tropical rainforests grow mostly close to the equator, in the Amazon and the Congo basin.» What does the Congo basin describe? | A kind of bowl | A rainforest animal | A sink | *An area of land drained by a river
exam: A basin can be a bowl, a sink, or land drained by a river. Which meaning fits «rain from a huge area flows into one great river»? | A bathroom sink | A harbour where ships park | *The land drained by a river | A pudding bowl
